        "created_at": "2012-08-22T17:37:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Or maybe you could play that if you draw a trap, rather than shuffling it randomly back into the deck, you could always place it face-up a certain number of spaces down in the deck, i.e. a trap will always go off three (for example) draws after it's first encountered.</p>",
